WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.811
"How will we defeat Sun Wukong?" moaned the Jade Emperor.

2
00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:10.099
"I sent our entire army, and they couldn't arrest him!"

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:16.445
"Perhaps we can ask the sage Erlang to capture him," said Guanyin.

4
00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:22.484
"Yes," said the Jade Emperor. "Erlang is very powerful."

5
00:00:22.485 --> 00:00:24.877
He turned back to the messenger.

6
00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:26.855
[g@"Go to Plum Mountain.

7
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:32.912
Ask Erlang if he'll help us."@g]

8
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:39.496
Wukong stood in front of the waterfall with his cheering subjects.

9
00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:45.389
"Our king has just defeated an entire army from Heaven!" said the gibbon.

10
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.483
"I hope the Jade Emperor learned his lesson," said Wukong.

11
00:00:49.484 --> 00:00:51.861
"He and his army are no match for—"

12
00:00:51.862 --> 00:00:56.636
"Sun Wukong!" a deep voice boomed.

13
00:00:56.637 --> 00:00:58.997
[g@Wukong looked up.

14
00:00:58.998 --> 00:01:02.880
A large man was coming down from the sky.@g]

15
00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:09.207
The apes and other monkeys ran and hid.

16
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:12.169
[g@"I am Erlang," said the man.

17
00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.972
"The Jade Emperor sent me to arrest you."@g]

18
00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:22.341
Wukong laughed. "The Jade Emperor's entire army couldn't defeat me.

19
00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:24.947
What do you think you're going to do?"

20
00:01:24.948 --> 00:01:28.886
"I am going to take you back to Heaven," said Erlang.

21
00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:32.184
"And you will be punished!"

22
00:01:32.185 --> 00:01:38.441
Waving his iron bar, Wukong leaped at Erlang.

23
00:01:38.442 --> 00:01:44.261
[i@Clang!@i] Erlang blocked the bar with his sword and then struck back.

24
00:01:44.262 --> 00:01:48.553
Wukong jumped onto a cloud to get out of the way.

25
00:01:48.554 --> 00:01:53.465
Erlang leaped into the air.

26
00:01:53.466 --> 00:01:57.357
He shook his body and suddenly grew much bigger.

27
00:01:57.358 --> 00:02:02.515
Wukong laughed. "I can do that too!"

28
00:02:02.516 --> 00:02:11.603
He shook his body and grew just as big as Erlang.

29
00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:16.845
Clouds swirled and wind blew as the two giants fought in the sky.

30
00:02:16.846 --> 00:02:20.751
Their weapons banged together all through the night.

31
00:02:20.752 --> 00:02:25.580
They were still fighting when the sun rose the next morning.

32
00:02:25.581 --> 00:02:29.412
"This fight could last forever," thought Wukong.

33
00:02:29.413 --> 00:02:32.186
"I should try a different plan."

34
00:02:32.187 --> 00:02:40.983
Wukong struck at Erlang one last time and then jumped back down to Earth.

35
00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:45.665
He turned himself into a sparrow and perched on a branch.

36
00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:49.739
"Erlang will never find me now," thought Wukong.

37
00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.354
[g@He looked up and saw a hawk.

38
00:02:52.355 --> 00:02:54.969
The hawk swooped toward him.@g]

39
00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:59.132
"Oh no!" thought Wukong. "That's Erlang!"

40
00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.243
Wukong dived into a stream.

41
00:03:03.244 --> 00:03:07.932
He turned himself into a fish and swam in the water.

42
00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:12.219
But then a crane flew over the stream.

43
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.854
[g@The crane swooped down at the water.

44
00:03:14.855 --> 00:03:17.307
Its mouth was wide open.@g]

45
00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:20.685
Wukong shot out of the stream.

46
00:03:20.686 --> 00:03:26.032
He changed back into himself and ran down a hill.

47
00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:29.268
"I'll turn myself into a temple," he thought.

48
00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:37.125
"Then, if Erlang tries to enter, I'll bite him!"

49
00:03:37.126 --> 00:03:42.642
Wukong's eyes became windows, and his mouth became a door.

50
00:03:42.643 --> 00:03:46.127
He turned his tail into a flagpole.

51
00:03:46.128 --> 00:03:50.001
A moment later Erlang came down the hill.

52
00:03:50.002 --> 00:03:53.633
When he saw the temple, he scratched his head.

53
00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:56.066
[g@"Hmm," said Erlang.

54
00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:59.553
"I never saw a temple with a flagpole before.@g]

55
00:03:59.554 --> 00:04:02.020
[g@This must be Wukong.

56
00:04:02.021 --> 00:04:04.805
I'll kick in that door."@g]

57
00:04:04.806 --> 00:04:09.544
"Oh no!" thought Wukong. "He'll break all my teeth!"

58
00:04:09.545 --> 00:04:14.319
[g@Wukong changed back into himself and ran.

59
00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:19.188
Erlang was right behind him.@g]

60
00:04:19.189 --> 00:04:26.030
Up in Heaven the Jade Emperor, the queen, and Guanyin watched the chase.

61
00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.879
The sage Laozi came over to them.

62
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.459
"What's going on?" he asked, looking down.

63
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:39.380
"That monkey, Sun Wukong, ate all the peaches from the garden," said the Jade Emperor.

64
00:04:39.381 --> 00:04:42.269
[g@"Then he defeated our entire army.

65
00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:45.724
Erlang is trying to catch him now."@g]

66
00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:48.602
"I can help," said Laozi.

67
00:04:48.603 --> 00:04:53.275
He took a metal ring off his arm.

68
00:04:53.276 --> 00:05:01.675
He aimed carefully and hurled it down to Earth.

69
00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:05.170
[i@Clunk!@i] The ring hit Wukong on the head.

70
00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:12.855
The monkey looked dizzy for a moment and then fell to the ground.

